                                    <h2><span class="shaft"><img id="674-0" src="//cdn.recordinghacks.com/images/icons/patterns/icon_8.png" width=27 height=27 alt="Bidirectional" title="Bidirectional" ></span>TNC Audio ACM-2</h2>
                    
                    <h2 class="sub">                    Bidirectional Ribbon Microphone</h2>
                    <p>The ACM-2 is a passive ribbon microphone with a 45mm aluminum ribbon. It appears to be another ShuaiYin SYR-30 clone, and is most likely identical to the t.bone RM700 and Nady RSM-4.</p><p>The large headbasket measures 3&#39;&#39; in diameter. The body diameter is ~7/8&#39;&#39; (22mm).</p><p><a rel="nofollow" href="http://www.flickr.com/photos/24455487@N05/3128515317/" title="TnC Audio ACM-2 Microphone by recordinghacks, on Flickr"><img src="http://farm4.static.flickr.com/3293/3128515317_3b009f9d71_m.jpg" width="200" alt="TnC Audio ACM-2 Microphone" class="thumb shaft" /></a>There is no circuit board or chassis under the body. The three screws nearest the head detach the capsule assembly and reveal the transformer; the bottom set of screws hold the XLR jack in place.</p><p><a rel="nofollow" href="http://www.flickr.com/photos/24455487@N05/3128515253/" title="TnC Audio ACM-2 Microphone by recordinghacks, on Flickr"><img src="http://farm4.static.flickr.com/3223/3128515253_70b4acdc40_m.jpg" height="200" alt="TnC Audio ACM-2 Microphone" class="thumb shaft" /></a>The front and back grilles are flat, rather than bowed (as in some SYR-30 derivatives). </p><p>Three layers of screening protect the ribbon element from blasts: the heavy outer grille (visible in the photos), a medium gauge layer of metal mesh just under the outer grille, and a layer of fine mesh mounted to the ribbon motor, covering just the ribbon.<br /> <br />The ACM-2 ships in a padded wooden storage case with a plastic mic clip.<p>The <a href="//recordinghacks.com/microphones/TnC-Audio/ACM-2">TNC Audio ACM-2</a> is also known as: ACM2.</p><p>The mic was released in 2008.</p>
